7}\\protected@file@percent }\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:3:  \"request_id\": \"verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:6:  \"claim\": \"Assemble verified facts to answer the 2D Maxwell-PML energy-functional goal with an alpha=1 obstruction plus Gronwall estimate and fractional case postponed.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:10:  \"summary\": \"The assembly is mostly supported by the cited verified facts: the alpha=1 source-model balance, PEC cancellation, polarization energy, magnetic shift, exact edge-PML linear-growth obstruction, and the positive augmented Gronwall estimate all trace to accepted fact verifications. The fractional postponement is also consistent with the edge obstruction because that obstruction occurs with P=0. However, the terminal report overclaims the exact list of Gronwall possible-growth terms: differentiating the displayed augmented energy also produces a sign-indefinite P P_{z,2} term from the P_{z,2} auxiliary norm, so the report's 'exactly' list is incomplete.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:18:  \"repair_hints\": \"Repair the Positive Gronwall energy section by displaying the full derivative of E_0 or by adding the missing P P_{z,2} mixed term to the list of sign-indefinite terms handled by Young's inequality. After that correction, the cited verified facts support the alpha=1 obstruction, Gronwall estimate, and fractional-case postponement.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:20:    \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/request.json\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:34:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-balance\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:35:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:edge-pml-linear-obstruction\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:36:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:augmented-gronwall-energy\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:37:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:run-20260619T173930696222Z:source-problem\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:44:  \"agent_run_dir\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:45:  \"agent_log\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/codex.log\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:46:  \"agent_events_log\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/codex.events.jsonl\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:47:  \"agent_stderr_log\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/codex.stderr.log\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:48:  \"agent_log_manifest\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T182155152008Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/log_manifest.json\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-.json:10:  \"summary\": \"Correct. The cited proof's edge-PML construction matches the source alpha=1 Maxwell-PML equations. For constant sigma_x=s>0, sigma_y=0, the ansatz E=P=P_{z,1}=P_{z,2}=H_y=Q_y=0 with spatially constant H_x,Q_x satisfies the electric equation, the alpha=1 polarization law, the P_z equations, the H_y/Q_y equations, and PEC. The remaining source equations reduce to H_{x,t}=bH_x+Q_x/mu and Q_{x,t}=-bQ_x-mu b^2H_x with b=s/epsilon_0, so M_x=Q_x+mu bH_x is conserved and nonzero M_x gives linear growth of H_x and Q_x. The symmetric sigma_x=0, sigma_y=s>0 construction gives the same conclusion for H_y,Q_y. Since these are exact finite-energy solutions whose displayed magnetic/auxiliary variables grow linearly, any time-independent positive coercive energy controlling the displayed variables cannot be monotone decreasing or uniformly long-time bounded for all source-system data in the edge-PML regime. The predecessor alpha=1 algebra-balance fact is verified and agrees with the source equations.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-.json:24:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:edge-pml-linear-obstruction\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-.json:25:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-balance\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-.json:26:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:run-20260619T173930696222Z:source-problem\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-.json:32:  \"claim_ceiling_after_verification\": \"verified\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet.json:6:  \"claim\": \"Strict decay of total electromagnetic-Debye energy on the whole computational domain is impossible without a nullspace, because nonzero stationary gradient magnetic fields can live in an undamped physical subregion with E=P=0 and zero dissipation.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet.json:10:  \"summary\": \"Correct. The source model and the repaired ADE model both use the 2D TM first-order evolution equations with E, H_x, H_y, P and PML auxiliaries, and the source problem imposes PEC E=0 but no additional divergence constraint. In an open physical subregion where sigma_x=sigma_y=0, choose phi smooth, compactly supported there, with grad phi nonzero, set E=P=0, all auxiliary variables zero, H_x=partial_x phi, and H_y=partial_y phi. Then partial_x H_y - partial_y H_x=0, partial_x E=partial_y E=0, the Debye law gives P_t=0, and every PML/ADE damping or auxiliary source term vanishes. Compact support keeps boundary and interface traces harmless. Thus the state is a nonzero stationary solution with positive magnetic energy for any positive state energy controlling H. Along such a stationary state an autonomous total electromagnetic-Debye energy cannot strictly decrease for every nonzero state. Therefore a valid dissipative identity on the whole computational domain must allow a nullspace containing these undamped curl-free magnetic modes.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet.json:20:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet.json:23:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet.json:28:  \"claim_ceiling_after_verification\": \"verified\",\n./artifacts/proofs/stage2_repair_design.md:7:- `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-a