 replacing partial_x by S_x^{-1} partial_x gives (S_x^{-1} kappa_sc)^2=kappa_0^2, so choosing the outgoing/decaying branch kappa_sc=S_x kappa_0 makes the PML admittance equal to the physical admittance and the reflection coefficient vanishes. The reduced normal-incidence system follows by multiplying the 1D stretched equations by (s+rho)/s, giving (partial_t+rho)(epsilon0 epsilon_infty E+P)=partial_x H_y, mu(partial_t+rho)H_y=partial_x E, and P+tau P_t=chi E. Multiplying by E and H_y and using E=(P+tau P_t)/chi yields exactly the stated energy derivative with the boundary flux plus the nonpositive bulk terms. The supporting artifact also correctly limits the result: it does not claim a full 2D monotone energy for the exact ADE stretched-coordinate system.\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m.json:24:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m.json:25:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:run-20260619T173930696222Z:source-problem\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m.json:28:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m.json:33:  \"claim_ceiling_after_verification\": \"verified\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:13:      \"location\": \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy\",\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:14:      \"issue\": \"referenced fact status is 'submitted', not 'verified'\"\n./verification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-