tched\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:7:  - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:8:status: verified\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:10:review_level: verified\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:12:claim_summary: \"The v2 covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye layer is not perfectly matched.\"\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:18:For a planar x-interface with constant layer coefficient rho_x=rho>0, rho_y=0, Laplace parameter Re s>0, and tangential Fourier number k_y, the physical Maxwell-Debye admittance is Y0^2=A(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2), where A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s).  The v2 covariantly damped model has Yrho^2=A_rho(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s(s+rho)), where A_rho(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau(s+rho)).  Hence Yrho^2-Y0^2=-rho[chi tau/(mu(1+tau(s+rho))(1+tau s))+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+rho))], which is generically nonzero.  Therefore the interface reflection coefficient (Y0-Yrho)/(Y0+Yrho) is generically nonzero: the model is dissipative but not perfectly matched.  Full derivation: artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md.\n./verification/requests/verify-20260619T183134018854Z-goal_success-analyze-sources-energy_func.json:11:    \"verification/results/verify-20260619T182724786704Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json\"\n./references/references.bib:58:  author = {Baffet, Daniel H. and Grote, Marcus J. and Imperiale, S{\\'e}bastien and Kachanovska, Maryna},\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md:2:fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md:7:status: verified\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md:9:review_level: verified\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md:17:If a physical subregion has zero PML damping, then E=0, P=0, all PML auxiliary variables zero, and H=(H_x,H_y)=grad phi with phi smooth and compactly supported in that undamped physical subregion gives an exact stationary Maxwell-Debye solution whenever curl H=partial_x H_y-partial_y H_x=0. The magnetic energy is positive for grad phi nonzero while all layer and Debye damping terms vanish. Hence no positive total energy controlling the magnetic field can be strictly decreasing for every nonzero state on the whole computational domain; any dissipative identity must have a characterized nullspace containing such undamped stationary modes. See artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md.\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T072508563237Z-fact-a-baffet-type-time-primitive-standa.json:7:  \"claim\": \"A Baffet-type time-primitive standard stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML has a full 2D constant-coefficient dissipative energy identity and remains Laplace-equivalent to the exact stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML.\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T072508563237Z-fact-a-baffet-type-time-primitive-standa.json:16:    \"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:baffet-primitive-stretched-debye-2d-energy\"\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:3:  \"request_id\": \"verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:7:  \"claim\": \"Assemble verified facts to answer the second-stage 2D Maxwell-PML energy design goal: identify the old edge-PML obstruction, compare compatibility/shifted/modified repairs, and present a verified repaired absorbing model with a monotone energy identity.\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:14:  \"prompt_path\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/prompt.md\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:15:  \"codex_log\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/codex.log\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:16:  \"codex_events\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/codex.events.jsonl\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:17:  \"codex_stderr\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/codex.stderr.log\",\n./verification/requests/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:18:  \"codex_log_manifest\": \"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ/log_manifest.json\"\n./tex/new_energy_functional_2d_debye_pml.toc:12:\\contentsline {section}{\\numberline {6}选定模型：Baffet 型 primitive Maxwell--Debye PML}{8}{section.6}%\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-augmented-gronwall-energy.md:2:fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:augmented-gronwall-energy\n./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-augmented-gronwall-energy.md:7:  - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-