ional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md\",\"resubmit\":false,\"reindexed\":true}}\n./memory/scratch/events.jsonl:32:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-20T06:47:56.820872Z\",\"channel\":\"events\",\"record\":{\"event_type\":\"fact_promote\",\"fact_id\":\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched\",\"path\":\"memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md\",\"status\":\"verified\",\"verification\":\"verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-c�若公式提取不完整，本报告只使用\\n可读的模型结构或自己重新推导的代数，不引用不可读公式作为证据。\\n\\n| 文献或文件 | 检查位置 | 读到的相关内容 | 本报告中的用途 |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `sources/energy_functional_problem.tex` | 全文，特别是模型与任务段 | 给出原八变量 Maxwell--PML/Cole--Cole 模型、PEC、\\\\(\\\\alpha=1\\\\) Debye 化、旧模型 \\\\(M_x,M_y\\\\) 变量与 fallback 要求。 | 定义旧模型和必须处理的 obstruction。 |\\n| `results/energy_functional_report_verified.md` | 全文 | 已验证旧模型能量代数、edge-PML 线性增长、Gronwall fallback。 | 作为旧模型背景，不替代新的 matching 推导。 |\\n| `results/energy_design_v2_report.md` 和 `_verified.md` | 全文 | v2 协变阻尼模型有正单调能量；perfect matching 明确未证明。 | 提供要测试的 v2 模型和已验证能量。 |\\n| `references/references.bib` | 全文 | Berenger、Joly/Becache、Baffet、dispersive PML、CFS/ADE、MPML 文献索引。 | 避免杜撰引用和题名。 |\\n| Joly 2012 | PDF pp. 6--8, 15--17 | PML 的本质是阻抗匹配/零反射；通过复坐标变换构造；二维中只应拉伸 PML 方向导数；简单各向同性阻尼一般不匹配。 | 定义本文的平面界面导纳测试。 |\\n| Bécache--Kachanovska--Wess 2023 | PDF pp. 6--8 | 色散波导 PML 在 Laplace 域先消去极化，采用 \\\\(1+\\\\sigma/(s\\\\zeta(s))\\\\) 伸缩；\\\\(\\\\zeta\\\\) 和 admissibility 影响稳定性。 | 支持“保留 \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\)，不要改成 \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_D(s+\\\\rho)\\\\)”的修复方向。 |\\n| Baffet--Grote--Imperiale--Kachanovska 2019 | PDF pp. 4--11 | 二阶波方程 PML 的单调能量不是朴素能量，而是含 shifted/time-integrated 变量的 augmented energy；常系数是清晰能量恒等式的自然范围。 | 指出完整二维 stretched PML 能量需要 Baffet 型结构。 |\\n| Bécache--Fliss--Kachanovska--Kazakova 2021 | PDF pp. 2--8 | 3D 对角各向异性 Maxwell 中 classical Cartesian PML 可能因 backward waves 不稳定。 | 强调 perfect matching 和 stability 是不同性质。 |\\n| Huang--Li--Liu 2023 | PDF pp. 1--6 | 等价 Berenger PML 的稳定性分析非平凡；变量阻尼情形仍困难。 | 支持“不能从匹配性自动推出朴素能量单调”。 |\\n| Meza-Fajardo--Papageorgiou 2008 | PDF pp. 1--2, 26 | M-PML 通过多轴阻尼改善稳定性；稳定性与阻尼比例相关。 | 作为 MPML 候选的背景。 |\\n| Correia--Jin 2006 | PDF pp. 1--5 | regular PML、CFS-PML、second-order PML 对传播波/倏逝波/低频表现不同。 | 作为 CFS/ADE 候选背景，不作为能量证明。 |\\n| Feng--Li 2013 | PDF pp. 1--4 | 高阶 stretched-coordinate PML 可用 ADE 实现，结合 CFS 优点。 | 支持 rational stretch 的 ADE 实现。 |\\n| Ping--Xu--Mao--Yang 2014 | PDF pp. 1--3, 8--10 | second-order M-PML 在弹性长时间计算中稳定有效。 | 支持 MPML 是稳定性修复类。 |\\n| Xie--Zheng--Cristini--Zhang 2023 | PDF pp. 1--7, 13 | 频移多轴 PML 提升吸收/稳定性；文中明确多轴界面不完全匹配。 | 用于标注 MPML 为 absorbing/stability 而非 exact matching。 |\\n| `references/main.pdf` | PDF pp. 45--47 等 | 本地笔记给出 stretched-coordinate 与 UPML 的相似性、Cole--Cole/UPML 频域形式。 | 项目背景；不可读公式不作为独立证据。 |\\n| `references/Super.pdf` | PDF pp. 20--25 | 本地超收敛笔记复述二维 C-CPML 频域/时域形式和能量稳定框架。 | 项目背景；不支持新 matching 结论。 |\\n| `references/Thesis.pdf` | PDF pp. 144--147 | 二维 C-CPML 中磁场方程的 \\\\((\\\\sigma_y-\\\\sigma_x)H_x\\\\)、\\\\((\\\\sigma_x-\\\\sigma_y)H_y\\\\) 使单调能量困难，只证明有限时间有界。 | 支持旧 C-CPML/八变量模型的能量困难分类。 |\\n\\n## 3. Perfect matching criterion\\n\\n设物理半空间为 \\\\(x<0\\\\)，PML 半空间为 \\\\(x>0\\\\)。取 Laplace--Fourier 模式\\n\\\\[\\nE,H,P\\\\sim e^{st+ik_y y+\\\\nu x},\\\\qquad \\\\Re s>0.\\n\\\\]\\n物理 Maxwell--Debye 介质满足\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau sP=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\varepsilon_D(s)=\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau s}.\\n\\\\]\\n物理方程为\\n\\\\[\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)E=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad \\\\mu sH_y=\\\\partial_xE.\\n\\\\]\\n代入 \\\\(\\\\partial_x=\\\\nu_0,\\\\partial_y=ik_y\\\\)，得到\\n\\\\[\\nH_x=-\\\\frac{ik_y}{\\\\mu s}E,\\\\qquad\\nH_y=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}E,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu_0^2=k_y^2+\\\\mu s^2\\\\varepsilon_D(s).\\n\\\\]\\n物理导纳定义为\\n\\\\[\\nY_0=\\\\frac{H_y}{E}=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\n对 \\\\(x=0\\\\) 界面，连续切向量为 \\\\(E\\\\) 与 \\\\(H_y\\\\)。若入射波振幅为 \\\\(1\\\\)，反射振幅为\\n\\\\(R\\\\)，透射振幅为 \\\\(T\\\\)，则\\n\\\\[\\n1+R=T,\\\\qquad Y_0(1-R)=Y_+T.\\n\\\\]\\n因此\\n\\\\[\\nR=\\\\frac{Y_0-Y_+}{Y_0+Y_+}.\\n\\\\]\\nperfect matching 的公式判据是\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{Y_+(s,k_y)=Y_0(s,k_y)\\\\quad\\\\text{对所有出射物理模成立}.}\\n\\\\]\\n\\n标准 stretched-coordinate PML 取\\n\\\\[\\nS_x(s)=1+\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x}{s}\\n\\\\]\\n并替换\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\partial_x\\\\mapsto S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x,\\n\\\\]\\n同时保持 \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\) 不变。于是 PML 中 \\\\(\\\\nu_+=S_x\\\\nu_0\\\\)，而\\n\\\\[\\nY_+=\\\\frac{S_x^{-1}\\\\nu_+}{\\\\mu s}\\n=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}=Y_0.\\n\\\\]\\n这就是本报告采用的匹配测试。\\n\\n## 4. Perfect matching test for the v2 model\\n\\nv2 模型为\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty D_\\\\rho E\\n=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x-D_\\\\rho P,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_y)H_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x)H_y=\\\\partial_xE,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau D_\\\\rho P=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad D_\\\\rho=\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho,\\\\quad\\n\\\\rho=\\\\rho_x+\\\\rho_y.\\n\\\\]\\n\\n考虑 \\\\(x\\\\)-PML 常系数半空间：\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\rho_x=\\\\rho>0,\\\\qquad \\\\rho_y=0.\\n\\\\]\\n则\\n\\\\[\\nP=\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)}E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)\\n=\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)}.\\n\\\\]\\nLaplace--Fourier 代数系统是\\n\\\\[\\n(s+\\\\rho)\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)E=\\\\nu H_y-ik_yH_x,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-ik_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)H_y=\\\\nu E.\\n\\\\]\\n所以\\n\\\\[\\nH_x=-\\\\frac{ik_y}{\\\\mu s}E,\\\\qquad\\nH_y=\\\\frac{\\\\nu}{\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)}E,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu^2=\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)^2\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+k_y^2\\\\frac{s+\\\\rho}{s}.\\n\\\\]\\nv2 透射导纳为\\n\\\\[\\nY_{v2}^2\\n=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left(\\n\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+\\\\frac{k_y^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}\\n\\\\right).\\n\\\\]\\n与\\n\\\\[\\nY_0^2\\n=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left(\\n\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+\\\\frac{k_y^2}{s^2}\\n\\\\right)\\n\\\\]\\n比较，得到精确失配\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\nY_{v2}^2-Y_0^2\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left[\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mu\\\\chi\\\\tau}{(1+\\\\tau s)(1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho))}\\n+\\\\frac{k_y^2}{s^2(s+\\\\rho)}\\n\\\\right].}\\n\\\\]\\n\\n因此 v2 不满足 \\\\(Y_{v2}=Y_0\\\\)。特别地：\\n\\n- 即使 \\\\(k_y=0\\\\)，只要 \\\\(\\\\chi\\\\tau\\\\rho\\\\ne0\\\\)，Debye 极化率从\\n  \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\) 变成 \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)\\\\)，阻抗已改变。\\n- 即使 \\\\(\\\\chi=0\\\\)，只要 \\\\(k_y\\\\ne0\\\\)，斜入射项也从 \\\\(k_y^2/s^2\\\\) 变成\\n  \\\\(k_y^2/[s(s+\\\\rho)]\\\\)。\\n\\n结论：v2 的协变 Debye 阻尼有利于能量耗散，但破坏了标准 PML 的\\nstretched-coordinate 阻抗匹配。\\n\\n## 5. Candidate repaired PML models\\n\\n### 5.1 标准 stretched-coordinate Maxwell--Debye PML\\n\\n推荐的精确匹配修复模型在 Laplace 域写作\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\widehat E\\n=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x\\\\widehat H_y\\n-S_y^{-1}\\\\partial_y\\\\widehat H_x,}\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\mu s\\\\widehat H_x=-S_y^{-1}\\\\partial_y\\\\widehat E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu s\\\\widehat H_y=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x\\\\widehat E,}\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{(1+\\\\tau s)\\\\widehat P=\\\\chi\\\\widehat E.}\\n\\\\]\\n其中\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T070357651402Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results/codex.events.jsonl:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Stage-3 proof: perfect-matching test for the v2 covariantly damped model\\n\\nProblem id: `2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration`\\n\\nTask: `task-stage3-perfect-matching-test`\\n\\n## Assumptions and notation\\n\\nUse the alpha \\\\(=1\\\\) Maxwell--Debye material law in the physical region:\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau \\\\partial_t P=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\varepsilon_D(s)=\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau s}.\\n\\\\]\\nHere \\\\(s\\\\in\\\\mathbb C\\\\), \\\\(\\\\Re s>0\\\\), is the Laplace frequency, and all initial\\ndata are taken zero for the interface symbol calculation.\\n\\nConsider a planar interface \\\\(x=0\\\\).  The physical half-space is \\\\(x<0\\\\).\\nThe PML half-space is \\\\(x>0\\\\), with constant \\\\(x\\\\)-layer coefficient\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\rho_x=\\\\rho>0,\\\\qquad \\\\rho_y=0 .\\n\\\\]\\nUse the tangential Fourier ansatz \\\\(e^{s t+i k y+\\\\nu x}\\\\), so\\n\\\\(\\\\partial_y\\\\mapsto i k\\\\), \\\\(\\\\partial_x\\\\mapsto \\\\nu\\\\).  The square-root branch is\\nchosen by outgoing/decaying continuation from \\\\(\\\\Re s>0\\\\).\\n\\nFor an \\\\(x\\\\)-interface the continuous tangential traces are \\\\(E\\\\) and \\\\(H_y\\\\).\\nFor incident and reflected physical modes,\\n\\\\[\\nE=E_i+E_r,\\\\qquad H_y=Y_0(E_i-E_r),\\n\\\\]\\nand for the transmitted PML mode \\\\(H_y=Y_+E_t\\\\).  Hence\\n\\\\[\\nR=\\\\frac{E_r}{E_i}=\\\\frac{Y_0-Y_+}{Y_0+Y_+}.\\n\\\\]\\nThe model is perfectly matched at this interface iff \\\\(Y_+=Y_0\\\\) for every\\n\\\\(s\\\\) and \\\\(k\\\\).\\n\\n## Physical Maxwell--Debye admittance\\n\\nThe Laplace-domain physical equations are\\n\\\\[\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)E=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x,\\n\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu sH_y=\\\\partial_xE .\\n\\\\]\\nWith \\\\(\\\\partial_x=\\\\nu_0\\\\), \\\\(\\\\partial_y=ik\\\\),\\n\\\\[\\nH_x=-\\\\frac{ik}{\\\\mu s}E,\\\\qquad\\nH_y=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}E .\\n\\\\]\\nSubstitution gives\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu_0^2=k^2+\\\\mu s^2\\\\varepsilon_D(s).\\n\\\\]\\nTherefore the physical admittance is\\n\\\\[\\nY_0(s,k)=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s},\\\\qquad\\nY_0(s,k)^2=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left(\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+\\\\frac{k^2}{s^2}\\\\right).\\n\\\\]\\n\\n## Standard stretched-coordinate check\\n\\nA classical \\\\(x\\\\)-PML has stretch factor\\n\\\\[\\nS_x(s)=1+\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x}{s}\\n\\\\]\\nand replaces \\\\(\\\\partial_x\\\\) by \\\\(S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x\\\\), while leaving the\\nphysical material law \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\) unchanged:\\n\\\\[\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)E=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x,\\n\\\\quad\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\quad\\n\\\\mu sH_y=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_xE.\\n\\\\]\\nFor a transmitted mode,\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu_+=S_x\\\\nu_0,\\\\qquad\\nY_+=\\\\frac{S_x^{-1}\\\\nu_+}{\\\\mu s}=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}=Y_0.\\n\\\\]\\nThus the stretched-coordinate model has \\\\(R=0\\\\) at the continuous planar\\ninterface.\\n\\n## v2 covariantly damped model\\n\\nThe v2 model is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty D_\\\\rho E\\n=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x-D_\\\\rho P,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_y)H_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x)H_y=\\\\partial_xE,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau D_\\\\rho P=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad\\nD_\\\\rho=\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x+\\\\rho_y.\\n\\\\]\\nIn the \\\\(x\\\\)-layer \\\\(\\\\rho_x=\\\\rho,\\\\rho_y=0\\\\), so\\n\\\\[\\nP=\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)}E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)=\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)} .\\n\\\\]\\nThe transformed equations are\\n\\\\[\\n(s+\\\\rho)\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)E=\\\\nu H_y-ikH_x,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-ikE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)H_y=\\\\nu E.\\n\\\\]\\nThus\\n\\\\[\\nH_x=-\\\\frac{ik}{\\\\mu s}E,\\\\qquad\\nH_y=\\\\frac{\\\\nu}{\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)}E\\n\\\\]\\nand\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu^2=\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)^2\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)\\n      +k^2\\\\frac{s+\\\\rho}{s}.\\n\\\\]\\nThe v2 PML admittance is therefore\\n\\\\[\\nY_{v2}(s,k)=\\\\frac{\\\\nu}{\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)},\\\\qquad\\nY_{v2}(s,k)^2\\n=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\n\\\\left(\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+\\\\frac{k^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}\\\\right).\\n\\\\]\\n\\nComparing with the physical admittance,\\n\\\\[\\nY_{v2}^2-Y_0^2\\n=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left[\\n\\\\mu(\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)-\\\\varepsilon_D(s))\\n+\\\\frac{k^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}-\\\\frac{k^2}{s^2}\\\\right].\\n\\\\]\\nSince\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)-\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\chi\\\\tau\\\\rho}{(1+\\\\tau s)(1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho))}\\n\\\\]\\nand\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{1}{s(s+\\\\rho)}-\\\\frac{1}{s^2}\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{s^2(s+\\\\rho)},\\n\\\\]\\nthe exact mismatch is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\nY_{v2}^2-Y_0^2\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left[\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mu\\\\chi\\\\tau}{(1+\\\\tau s)(1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho))}\\n+\\\\frac{k^2}{s^2(s+\\\\rho)}\\n\\\\right].}\\n\\\\]\\nThis expression is not identically zero for \\\\(\\\\rho>0\\\\).  Hence the v2 model is\\nnot perfectly matched.\\n\\nThe corresponding reflection coefficient is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\nR_{v2}(s,k)=\\n\\\\frac{\\n\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+k^2/s^2}\\n-\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+k^2/[s(s+\\\\rho)]}\\n}{\\n\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+k^2/s^2}\\n+\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+k^2/[s(s+\\\\rho)]}\\n}.}\\n\\\\]\\nThe square-root branches are those inherited from the outgoing physical and\\ndecaying PML modes.\\n\\n## Interpretation of the mismatch\\n\\nThere are two independent formula-level defects.\\n\\n1. The Debye susceptibility is shifted from\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau s}\\n\\\\quad\\\\text{to}\\\\quad\\n\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)}.\\n\\\\]\\nThis changes the material impedance even at normal incidence \\\\(k=0\\\\), unless\\n\\\\(\\\\chi=0\\\\), \\\\(\\\\tau=0\\\\), or \\\\(\\\\rho=0\\\\).\\n\\n2. The oblique tangential part changes from \\\\(k^2/s^2\\\\) to\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{k^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}.\\n\\\\]\\nThis remains a mismatch for \\\\(k\\\\ne0\\\\) even in the nondispersive limit\\n\\\\(\\\\chi=0\\\\).\\n\\nThus applying the same covariant derivative \\\\(D_\\\\rho\\\\) to the Debye law is good\\nfor the v2 monotone energy identity, but it is not the Laplace-domain\\nstretched-coordinate continuation of the physical Maxwell--Debye system.\\n\\n## Durable fact candidate\\n\\nClaim summary:\\nThe covariantly damped v2 Maxwell--Debye absorbing-layer model is not perfectly\\nmatched at a planar constant-coefficient \\\\(x\\\\)-PML interface; its squared\\nadmittance differs from the physical Maxwell--Debye admittance by the boxed\\nformula above.\\n\\nDependencies:\\n\\n- `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy`\\n  for the v2 model definition and verified energy identity.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T070357651402Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results/codex.events.jsonl:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Stage-3 Literature Reading Record\\n\\nProblem id: `2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration`\\n\\nScope: readings used for the stage-3 perfect-matching and dissipative-energy\\nanalysis.  Page numbers for PDFs are the extractor/PDF page numbers unless an\\ninternal printed page number is explicitly visible.  Some mathematical displays\\nin the local PDFs are only partially represented by `pdfminer`; in those cases I\\nuse the surrounding prose and section labels only, and derive the algebra in the\\nstage-3 proof artifacts rather than quoting unreadable formulas.\\n\\n| Source | Inspected location | Relevant result observed | Use in stage 3 |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `sources/energy_functional_problem.tex` | Full source, especially Sections 2--7 and deliverables | Defines the original eight-variable Maxwell--PML/Cole--Cole problem, PEC boundary condition, alpha \\\\(=1\\\\) Debye reduction, shifted \\\\(M_x,M_y\\\\) identities to check, and requested obstruction/fallback structure. | Establishes the baseline old model and the verified edge-mode obstruction that any repaired model must address. |\\n| `results/energy_functional_report_verified.md` | Full verified report | Verified alpha \\\\(=1\\\\) algebra, old-model edge PML linear growth \\\\(M_x=\\\\mathrm{const}\\\\), and augmented Gronwall estimate. | Reused only as verified old-model context, not as a substitute for the new matching derivation. |\\n| `results/energy_design_v2_report.md` and `_verified.md` | Full stage-2 report | The covariantly damped Maxwell--Debye layer has a positive monotone energy, but exact perfect matching was explicitly left open. | Supplies the model to test and the previously verified energy identity. |\\n| `references/references.bib` | Full file | Bibliographic map for Berenger, Joly/Becache, Baffet, dispersive PML, CFS/ADE, MPML, and local manuscripts. | Used to avoid inventing references and to align local PDFs with citation keys. |\\n| Joly (2012), elementary PML introduction | PDF pp. 6--7, 9--11, 14--17, 19--20 | PML is characterized by impedance matching/zero reflection; construction via complex coordinate change \\\\(x\\\\mapsto x+(i\\\\omega)^{-1}\\\\int\\\\sigma\\\\); in 2D only the derivative in the PML direction is stretched; adding isotropic damping to all components is not generally perfectly matched. | Defines the planar-interface/stretched-coordinate test used in the v2 mismatch proof. |\\n| Baffet--Grote--Imperiale--Kachanovska (2019) | PDF pp. 4--11 and 35 | For the second-order wave PML, a non-naive augmented energy with shifted variables and time integrals decays for constant damping; variable/piecewise damping introduces gradient/interface remainders, so monotone decay is not automatic. | Provides the model for what a genuine dissipative PML energy must contain and justifies constant-coefficient scope for sharp identities. |\\n| Bécache--Fliss--Kachanovska--Kazakova (2021) | PDF pp. 2--8 | Classical Cartesian PML for Maxwell can become unstable in some anisotropic 3D diagonal media; stability is model-dependent and tied to backward waves/group velocity. | Used as a caution that perfect matching and stability are distinct properties. |\\n| Bécache--Kachanovska--Wess (2023) | PDF pp. 4--10 and references pp. 39--40 | For dispersive waveguides, the PML is derived in the Laplace domain after eliminating polarization; the stretch uses \\\\(1+\\\\sigma/(s\\\\zeta(s))\\\\). Material passivity/admissibility and the choice of \\\\(\\\\zeta\\\\) matter for stability; the paper gives a time-domain auxiliary-variable PML and exponential truncation error theorem. | Supports using the physical material law \\\\(A(s)\\\\) in the stretched-coordinate derivation, rather than replacing it by \\\\(A(s+\\\\rho)\\\\). |\\n| Huang--Li--Liu (2023) | PDF pp. 1--6 | Equivalent Berenger PML models have nontrivial stability analysis; an explicit unconditionally stable finite-element scheme is built for an equivalent model, while variable-damping energy stability remains difficult. | Used to classify equivalent Berenger/ADE systems as plausible but not automatically monotone in the simple \\\\(L^2\\\\) energy. |\\n| Meza-Fajardo--Papageorgiou (2008), local `A_Nonconvolutional...pdf` | PDF pp. 1--6, 8--10, 19, 23, 26 | M-PML adds damping in multiple coordinate directions; stability can improve, but it is a modified absorbing layer with parameters chosen for spectral stability. | Used for the MPML repair option and for the statement that stabilizing modifications can sacrifice exact perfect matching. |\\n| Correia--Jin (2006) | PDF pp. 1--5 | Regular PML, CFS-PML, and second-order PML have different absorption strengths; CFS helps evanescent waves but can hurt low-frequency propagating waves, while higher-order PML combines mechanisms. | Used for the CFS/ADE candidate classification, not as an energy proof. |\\n| Feng--Li (2013) | PDF pp. 1--4 and 6--9 | Higher-order stretched-coordinate PML can be implemented through ADE variables and can improve late-time/evanescent absorption in computations. | Used to justify an ADE time-domain realization of rational stretch factors. |\\n| Ping--Xu--Mao--Yang (2014) | PDF pp. 1--3 and 8--10 | Second-order M-PML is reported as long-time stable and efficient in elastic simulations, while classical PML can show late-time instability. | Used as supporting context for MPML as a stability-oriented, not exact-matching-first, repair class. |\\n| Xie--Zheng--Cristini--Zhang (2023) | PDF pp. 1--7 and 13 | M-PML is explicitly described as losing perfect matching because of multiaxial stretching, though frequency shifting improves near-grazing and long-time behavior. | Used to state that MPML-type repairs should be labeled stable/absorbing, not perfectly matched. |\\n| `references/main.pdf` | PDF pp. 4--6, 38--40, 42--48, 54--56 | Local manuscript derives UPML/Cole--Cole frequency-domain forms, 2D energy boundedness, stretched-coordinate PML notes, and CFS-PML attempts; formulas are partly unreadable in extraction. | Used as local project context; no independent formula claim is taken from unreadable displays. |\\n| `references/Super.pdf` | PDF pp. 1--5, 20, 30, 35--38 | Local superconvergence notes for DG methods with PML; mostly numerical-analysis context rather than continuous matching algebra. | Not used as support for perfect matching; recorded because it was requested among local PDFs. |\\n| `references/Thesis.pdf` | PDF pp. 80--86, 111--112, 144--149, 151--155 | Local thesis states one-dimensional C-CPML discrete energies can be strictly dissipative; two-dimensional C-CPML continuous stability is proved by a Gronwall estimate, with monotone energy difficult due to anisotropic PML magnetic terms. | Supports the report's distinction between 1D strict dissipation and 2D finite-time stability for the old C-CPML-style system. |\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T070357651402Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results/codex.events.jsonl:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,320p' artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Stage-3 proof: repaired PML candidates and dissipative-energy classification\\n\\nProblem id: `2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration`\\n\\nTask: `task-stage3-repaired-model-energy`\\n\\n## Input fact from the matching test\\n\\nThe v2 covariantly damped Maxwell--Debye model has the verified stage-2 monotone\\nenergy identity, but the stage-3 interface calculation shows that it is not a\\nperfectly matched layer.  In an \\\\(x\\\\)-layer with \\\\(\\\\rho_x=\\\\rho>0,\\\\rho_y=0\\\\),\\n\\\\[\\nY_{v2}^2-Y_0^2\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left[\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mu\\\\chi\\\\tau}{(1+\\\\tau s)(1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho))}\\n+\\\\frac{k_y^2}{s^2(s+\\\\rho)}\\n\\\\right],\\n\\\\]\\nso the v2 reflection coefficient is not identically zero.\\n\\nTherefore a repaired model must keep the physical Debye law as a function of the\\nLaplace variable \\\\(s\\\\), not \\\\(s+\\\\rho\\\\), and must implement damping through\\ncoordinate stretching or an equivalent split/ADE system.\\n\\n## Candidate 1: classical stretched-coordinate Maxwell--Debye PML\\n\\nLet\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\varepsilon_D(s)=\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau s},\\n\\\\qquad\\nS_i(s)=1+\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_i}{s},\\\\quad i=x,y.\\n\\\\]\\nIn the physical region \\\\(\\\\sigma_x=\\\\sigma_y=0\\\\).  In the PML the coefficients are\\nnonnegative and are first analyzed as piecewise constant near each planar\\ninterface.\\n\\nThe Laplace-domain repaired model is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\widehat E\\n=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x\\\\widehat H_y\\n-S_y^{-1}\\\\partial_y\\\\widehat H_x,}\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\mu s\\\\widehat H_x=-S_y^{-1}\\\\partial_y\\\\widehat E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu s\\\\widehat H_y=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x\\\\widehat E,}\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{(1+\\\\tau s)\\\\widehat P=\\\\chi\\\\widehat E.}\\n\\\\]\\nEquivalently, the Debye law is not damped:\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau P_t=\\\\chi E.\\n\\\\]\\n\\n### Perfect matching\\n\\nAt an \\\\(x\\\\)-interface, \\\\(S_y=1\\\\).  With tangential Fourier number \\\\(k_y\\\\),\\nthe physical normal symbol satisfies\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu_0^2=k_y^2+\\\\mu s^2\\\\varepsilon_D(s),\\\\qquad\\nY_0=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}.\\n\\\\]\\nIn the PML,\\n\\\\[\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D E=S_x^{-1}\\\\nu H_y-ik_yH_x,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-ik_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu sH_y=S_x^{-1}\\\\nu E.\\n\\\\]\\nThe dispersion relation gives\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\left(S_x^{-1}\\\\nu\\\\right)^2=k_y^2+\\\\mu s^2\\\\varepsilon_D(s),\\n\\\\]\\nhence \\\\(\\\\nu=S_x\\\\nu_0\\\\) and\\n\\\\[\\nY_+=\\\\frac{S_x^{-1}\\\\nu}{\\\\mu s}=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}=Y_0.\\n\\\\]\\nThus the planar-interface reflection coefficient is \\\\(R=0\\\\) for every\\n\\\\((s,k_y)\\\\) in the Laplace half-plane.  The same argument applies to a\\n\\\\(y\\\\)-interface with \\\\(x,y\\\\) interchanged.\\n\\n### Time-domain ADE realization\\n\\nDefine the causal operator\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal A_i=S_i^{-1}=\\\\frac{s}{s+\\\\sigma_i}\\n\\\\]\\nin the Laplace domain.  Equivalently,\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal A_i f=f+\\\\psi_i,\\\\qquad\\n(\\\\partial_t+\\\\sigma_i)\\\\psi_i=-\\\\sigma_i f.\\n\\\\]\\nThen a time-domain unsplit ADE form is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E_t+P_t\\n=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x\\n+\\\\psi_{E,x}-\\\\psi_{E,y},\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu H_{x,t}=-\\\\partial_yE-\\\\psi_{H_x,y},\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu H_{y,t}=\\\\partial_xE+\\\\psi_{H_y,x},\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau P_t=\\\\chi E,\\n\\\\]\\nwith\\n\\\\[\\n(\\\\partial_t+\\\\sigma_x)\\\\psi_{E,x}=-\\\\sigma_x\\\\partial_xH_y,\\\\qquad\\n(\\\\partial_t+\\\\sigma_y)\\\\psi_{E,y}=-\\\\sigma_y\\\\partial_yH_x,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n(\\\\partial_t+\\\\sigma_y)\\\\psi_{H_x,y}=-\\\\sigma_y\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n(\\\\partial_t+\\\\sigma_x)\\\\psi_{H_y,x}=-\\\\sigma_x\\\\partial_xE.\\n\\\\]\\nInterface conditions are continuity of the physical tangential traces.  For an\\n\\\\(x\\\\)-interface these are \\\\(E\\\\) and \\\\(H_y\\\\).  The auxiliary variables vanish in the\\nphysical region and are initialized consistently with the causal convolution.\\n\\n### Naive energy calculation\\n\\nThe natural physical Debye energy is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal E_{\\\\rm phys}\\n=\\\\frac12\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\n\\\\left(\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E^2+\\\\mu H_x^2+\\\\mu H_y^2+\\\\chi^{-1}P^2\\\\right)\\\\,dxdy.\\n\\\\]\\nIt is positive because\\n\\\\(\\\\epsilon_0,\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty,\\\\mu,\\\\chi>0\\\\).  Using\\n\\\\[\\nE P_t=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\chi}\\\\partial_t(P^2)+\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}P_t^2\\n\\\\]\\nand the PEC boundary condition \\\\(E=0\\\\) on the outer boundary gives\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{d}{dt}\\\\mathcal E_{\\\\rm phys}\\n=-\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}P_t^2\\\\,dxdy\\n+\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\n\\\\left[\\nE(\\\\psi_{E,x}-\\\\psi_{E,y})\\n-H_x\\\\psi_{H_x,y}\\n+H_y\\\\psi_{H_y,x}\\n\\\\right]\\\\,dxdy .\\n\\\\]\\nThe Maxwell principal part contributes only the boundary flux\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\int_{\\\\partial\\\\Omega}E(H_y n_x-H_x n_y)\\\\,ds,\\n\\\\]\\nwhich vanishes under PEC at the outer boundary and cancels by transmission at\\ninternal material/PML interfaces when the tangential traces are continuous.\\n\\nThe remaining auxiliary terms are not sign-definite in this naive energy.\\nTherefore the positive physical Debye energy alone is not a monotone energy for\\nthe exact stretched-coordinate PML.\\n\\n### Classification\\n\\nThis candidate is the formula-level perfect-matching repair.  A local monotone\\nenergy for the full 2D Maxwell--Debye ADE system is not certified here.  The\\ncalculation above identifies the exact terms that a Baffet-type augmented energy\\nwould have to absorb:\\n\\\\[\\nE\\\\psi_{E,x},\\\\quad E\\\\psi_{E,y},\\\\quad\\nH_x\\\\psi_{H_x,y},\\\\quad H_y\\\\psi_{H_y,x}.\\n\\\\]\\nThe literature record supports that such augmented energies are non-naive and\\nthat constant-coefficient damping is the natural first scope for a sharp identity.\\n\\n### Reduced normal-incidence 1D energy identity\\n\\nThere is one important positive result for the exact stretched-coordinate model.\\nIn the \\\\(x\\\\)-layer normal-incidence block \\\\(k_y=0\\\\), the standard stretch gives\\n\\\\[\\n(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho)(\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E+P)=\\\\partial_xH_y,\\n\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho)H_y=\\\\partial_xE,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau P_t=\\\\chi E.\\n\\\\]\\nThis is exactly the \\\\(k_y=0\\\\) restriction of the perfectly matched stretched\\nmodel, not the v2 model, because the Debye law still uses \\\\(\\\\partial_t\\\\) rather\\nthan \\\\(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho\\\\).\\n\\nMultiply the first equation by \\\\(E\\\\), the second by \\\\(H_y\\\\), and use\\n\\\\[\\nE=\\\\frac{P+\\\\tau P_t}{\\\\chi}.\\n\\\\]\\nThen\\n\\\\[\\nE P_t=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\chi}\\\\partial_t(P^2)+\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}P_t^2,\\n\\\\]\\nand\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\rho E P\\n=\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\chi}P^2+\\\\frac{\\\\rho\\\\tau}{2\\\\chi}\\\\partial_t(P^2).\\n\\\\]\\nAfter integrating by parts, the principal terms give only the boundary flux\\n\\\\(\\\\int_{\\\\partial I}EH_y n_x\\\\,ds\\\\).  Hence\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\frac{d}{dt}\\\\mathcal E_{1d,sc}\\n=-\\\\int_I\\\\left(\\n\\\\rho\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E^2+\\\\mu\\\\rho H_y^2\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\chi}P^2+\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}P_t^2\\n\\\\right)\\\\,dx\\n+\\\\int_{\\\\partial I}EH_y n_x\\\\,ds,}\\n\\\\]\\nwhere\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\mathcal E_{1d,sc}\\n=\\\\frac12\\\\int_I\\\\left(\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E^2+\\\\mu H_y^2\\n+\\\\frac{1+\\\\rho\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}P^2\\n\\\\right)\\\\,dx.}\\n\\\\]\\nThis energy is positive for \\\\(\\\\rho,\\\\tau,\\\\chi>0\\\\), and it is dissipative under\\nPEC or otherwise nonpositive boundary flux.  It explains why the v2 idea is\\nclose to a useful construction in normal incidence, but it does not solve the\\nfull 2D oblique problem: as soon as \\\\(k_y\\\\ne0\\\\), the exact stretched model\\ncontains the ADE memory couplings displayed above.\\n\\n## Candidate 2: generalized CFS/ADE stretched-coordinate PML\\n\\nLet\\n\\\\[\\nS_i(s)=\\\\kappa_i+\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_i}{s+\\\\alpha_i},\\n\\\\qquad\\n\\\\kappa_i\\\\ge1,\\\\quad \\\\sigma_i\\\\ge0,\\\\quad \\\\alpha_i\\\\ge0.\\n\\\\]\\nThe repaired Laplace-domain equations are the same as Candidate 1, with these\\n\\\\(S_i\\\\).  In particular the Debye law remains\\n\\\\[\\n(1+\\\\tau s)\\\\widehat P=\\\\chi\\\\widehat E.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nFor a planar \\\\(x\\\\)-interface with \\\\(S_y=1\\\\), the same calculation gives\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu=S_x\\\\nu_0,\\\\qquad Y_+=Y_0,\\n\\\\]\\nso the continuous model is perfectly matched whenever the stretch is applied to\\nthe spatial derivatives and the physical material law is left unchanged.\\n\\nIf \\\\(S_i^{-1}\\\\) is rational with poles in \\\\(\\\\Re s<0\\\\), it can be implemented by\\nADE variables.  The CFS shift \\\\(\\\\alpha_i>0\\\\) is a standard way to improve\\nlow-frequency/evanescent and late-time behavior, but a monotone time-domain\\nenergy requires an explicit positive realization of the memory kernel.  No such\\npositive memory theorem is claimed here for the full 2D Maxwell--Debye system.\\n\\nClassification: perfectly matched at the continuous planar-interface level;\\nrecommended if long-time CFS behavior is needed; energy status is boundedness or\\npassive-memory proof pending, not a completed monotone identity.\\n\\n## Candidate 3: MPML-type extra damping\\n\\nAn MPML-type repair adds damping in more than the normal coordinate direction.\\nFor example, in an \\\\(x\\\\)-layer one may replace a scalar stretch by a multiaxial\\nstretch depending also on tangential damping parameters.  This is useful for\\nremoving long-time instabilities or Jordan-block behavior in some systems.\\n\\nHowever, if the tangential stretch is nontrivial at the physical/PML interface,\\nthe planar admittance generally changes.  The MPML literature inspected for this\\nrun explicitly treats MPML as a stability-oriented absorbing layer and records\\nthat exact perfect matching may be lost in multiaxial variants.\\n\\nClassification: absorbing/stability repair, not the primary exact-matching\\nrepair for the present Maxwell--Debye interface theorem.\\n\\n## Complete dissipative identity that is currently verified\\n\\nThe only complete positive monotone identity verified in the existing Iteris\\nmemory is for the v2 covariantly damped absorbing layer:\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty D_\\\\rho E\\n=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x-D_\\\\rho P,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_y)H_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x)H_y=\\\\partial_xE,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau D_\\\\rho P=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad D_\\\\rho=\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x+\\\\rho_y.\\n\\\\]\\nIts energy is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal E_\\\\rho(t)=\\\\frac12\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\n\\\\left(\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E^2+\\\\mu H_x^2+\\\\mu H_y^2+\\\\chi^{-1}P^2\\\\right)\\\\,dxdy\\n\\\\]\\nand the verified identity is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{d}{dt}\\\\mathcal E_\\\\rho(t)\\n=-\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\\\left(\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty\\\\rho E^2\\n+\\\\mu\\\\rho_yH_x^2\\n+\\\\mu\\\\rho_xH_y^2\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\chi}P^2\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}|D_\\\\rho P|^2\\n\\\\right)\\\\,dxdy.\\n\\\\]\\nThis identity is genuinely dissipative, but the model is not perfectly matched.\\nIt should therefore be described as a stable absorbing-layer model, not as a\\nstandard PML.\\n\\n## Formula-level obstruction to strict decay on the whole domain\\n\\nEven for a perfectly matched repair, strict decay of a total energy controlling\\nall fields on the whole computational domain cannot hold without a nullspace.\\nAssume a physical subregion where \\\\(\\\\sigma_x=\\\\sigma_y=0\\\\) and choose\\n\\\\[\\nE=0,\\\\qquad P=0,\\\\qquad H_x=\\\\partial_x\\\\phi,\\\\qquad H_y=\\\\partial_y\\\\phi,\\n\\\\]\\nwith \\\\(\\\\phi\\\\) smooth and compactly supported inside that undamped physical\\nsubregion.  Then\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x=0,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\partial_yE=\\\\partial_xE=0,\\n\\\\]\\nand all PML auxiliary variables initialized at zero remain zero for at least this\\nexact stationary solution.  The magnetic energy is positive if \\\\(\\\\nabla\\\\phi\\\\ne0\\\\),\\nbut every damping term in the PML vanishes.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T070357651402Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results/codex.events.jsonl:23:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,280p' verification/results/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m.json\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"iteris.verification_result.v0\\\",\\n  \\\"request_id\\\": \\\"verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m\\\",\\n  \\\"backend\\\": \\\"agent\\\",\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The standard stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML restores planar-interface perfect matching and, in the reduced normal-incidence constant-coefficient case, has the dissipative energy identity stated in the fact file.\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"accepted\\\",\\n  \\\"passed\\\": true,\\n  \\\"strict_verdict\\\": \\\"correct\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Correct within the stated scope. The cited fact is supported for the standard Laplace-domain stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML with the physical Debye law left as A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s), coordinate-aligned planar interfaces, Re s>0, physical positive material parameters, and constant nonnegative layer damping in the reduced 1D energy calculation. The planar-interface calculation is algebraic: replacing partial_x by S_x^{-1} partial_x gives (S_x^{-1} kappa_sc)^2=kappa_0^2, so choosing the outgoing/decaying branch kappa_sc=S_x kappa_0 makes the PML admittance equal to the physical admittance and the reflection coefficient vanishes. The reduced normal-incidence system follows by multiplying the 1D stretched equations by (s+rho)/s, giving (partial_t+rho)(epsilon0 epsilon_infty E+P)=partial_x H_y, mu(partial_t+rho)H_y=partial_x E, and P+tau P_t=chi E. Multiplying by E and H_y and using E=(P+tau P_t)/chi yields exactly the stated energy derivative with the boundary flux plus the nonpositive bulk terms. The supporting artifact also correctly limits the result: it does not claim a full 2D monotone energy for the exact ADE stretched-coordinate system.\\\",\\n  \\\"critical_errors\\\": [],\\n  \\\"gaps\\\": [],\\n  \\\"repair_hints\\\": \\\"No repair needed.\\\",\\n  \\\"checked_artifacts\\\": [\\n    \\\"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m/request.json\\\",\\n    \\\"memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy.md\\\",\\n    \\\"artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md\\\",\\n    \\\"artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md\\\",\\n    \\\"sources/energy_functional_problem.tex\\\",\\n    \\\"artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md\\\",\\n    \\\"references/processed/Joly - 2012 - An elementary introduction to the construction and the analysis of perfectly matched layers for time.txt\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"checked_fact_ids\\\": [\\n    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy\\\",\\n    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:run-20260619T173930696222Z:source-problem\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"primary_fact_ids\\\": [\\n    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"target_artifact\\\": null,\\n  \\\"executor\\\": \\\"codex\\\",\\n  \\\"verification_scope\\\": \\\"codex_agent\\\",\\n  \\\"claim_