ell-Debye layer is not perfectly matched and gives a squared-admittance mismatch. I’m opening the cited fact file, proof artifact, and report now to check the derivation and scope.\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d/codex.events.jsonl:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\nfact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched\\nproblem_id: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration\\nsource_project: 2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration\\nsource_task: task-stage3-perfect-matching-test\\npredecessors:\\n  - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy\\nstatus: submitted\\nfact_type: obstruction\\nreview_level: none\\nclaim_policy: stable_claim\\nclaim_summary: \\\"The v2 covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye layer is not perfectly matched.\\\"\\nverification: null\\n---\\n\\n## statement\\n\\nFor a planar x-interface with constant layer coefficient rho_x=rho>0, rho_y=0, Laplace parameter Re s>0, and tangential Fourier number k_y, the physical Maxwell-Debye admittance is Y0^2=A(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2), where A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s).  The v2 covariantly damped model has Yrho^2=A_rho(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s(s+rho)), where A_rho(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau(s+rho)).  Hence Yrho^2-Y0^2=-rho[chi tau/(mu(1+tau(s+rho))(1+tau s))+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+rho))], which is generically nonzero.  Therefore the interface reflection coefficient (Y0-Yrho)/(Y0+Yrho) is generically nonzero: the model is dissipative but not perfectly matched.  Full derivation: artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md.\\n\\n## notes\\n\\nGenerated by Iteris bootstrap workflow.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d/codex.events.jsonl:16:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,320p' artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Stage-3 proof: perfect-matching test for the v2 covariantly damped model\\n\\nProblem id: `2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration`\\n\\nTask: `task-stage3-perfect-matching-test`\\n\\n## Assumptions and notation\\n\\nUse the alpha \\\\(=1\\\\) Maxwell--Debye material law in the physical region:\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau \\\\partial_t P=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\varepsilon_D(s)=\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau s}.\\n\\\\]\\nHere \\\\(s\\\\in\\\\mathbb C\\\\), \\\\(\\\\Re s>0\\\\), is the Laplace frequency, and all initial\\ndata are taken zero for the interface symbol calculation.\\n\\nConsider a planar interface \\\\(x=0\\\\).  The physical half-space is \\\\(x<0\\\\).\\nThe PML half-space is \\\\(x>0\\\\), with constant \\\\(x\\\\)-layer coefficient\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\rho_x=\\\\rho>0,\\\\qquad \\\\rho_y=0 .\\n\\\\]\\nUse the tangential Fourier ansatz \\\\(e^{s t+i k y+\\\\nu x}\\\\), so\\n\\\\(\\\\partial_y\\\\mapsto i k\\\\), \\\\(\\\\partial_x\\\\mapsto \\\\nu\\\\).  The square-root branch is\\nchosen by outgoing/decaying continuation from \\\\(\\\\Re s>0\\\\).\\n\\nFor an \\\\(x\\\\)-interface the continuous tangential traces are \\\\(E\\\\) and \\\\(H_y\\\\).\\nFor incident and reflected physical modes,\\n\\\\[\\nE=E_i+E_r,\\\\qquad H_y=Y_0(E_i-E_r),\\n\\\\]\\nand for the transmitted PML mode \\\\(H_y=Y_+E_t\\\\).  Hence\\n\\\\[\\nR=\\\\frac{E_r}{E_i}=\\\\frac{Y_0-Y_+}{Y_0+Y_+}.\\n\\\\]\\nThe model is perfectly matched at this interface iff \\\\(Y_+=Y_0\\\\) for every\\n\\\\(s\\\\) and \\\\(k\\\\).\\n\\n## Physical Maxwell--Debye admittance\\n\\nThe Laplace-domain physical equations are\\n\\\\[\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)E=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x,\\n\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu sH_y=\\\\partial_xE .\\n\\\\]\\nWith \\\\(\\\\partial_x=\\\\nu_0\\\\), \\\\(\\\\partial_y=ik\\\\),\\n\\\\[\\nH_x=-\\\\frac{ik}{\\\\mu s}E,\\\\qquad\\nH_y=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}E .\\n\\\\]\\nSubstitution gives\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu_0^2=k^2+\\\\mu s^2\\\\varepsilon_D(s).\\n\\\\]\\nTherefore the physical admittance is\\n\\\\[\\nY_0(s,k)=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s},\\\\qquad\\nY_0(s,k)^2=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left(\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+\\\\frac{k^2}{s^2}\\\\right).\\n\\\\]\\n\\n## Standard stretched-coordinate check\\n\\nA classical \\\\(x\\\\)-PML has stretch factor\\n\\\\[\\nS_x(s)=1+\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x}{s}\\n\\\\]\\nand replaces \\\\(\\\\partial_x\\\\) by \\\\(S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_x\\\\), while leaving the\\nphysical material law \\\\(\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\\\) unchanged:\\n\\\\[\\ns\\\\varepsilon_D(s)E=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x,\\n\\\\quad\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\quad\\n\\\\mu sH_y=S_x^{-1}\\\\partial_xE.\\n\\\\]\\nFor a transmitted mode,\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu_+=S_x\\\\nu_0,\\\\qquad\\nY_+=\\\\frac{S_x^{-1}\\\\nu_+}{\\\\mu s}=\\\\frac{\\\\nu_0}{\\\\mu s}=Y_0.\\n\\\\]\\nThus the stretched-coordinate model has \\\\(R=0\\\\) at the continuous planar\\ninterface.\\n\\n## v2 covariantly damped model\\n\\nThe v2 model is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty D_\\\\rho E\\n=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x-D_\\\\rho P,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_y)H_x=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x)H_y=\\\\partial_xE,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nP+\\\\tau D_\\\\rho P=\\\\chi E,\\\\qquad\\nD_\\\\rho=\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x+\\\\rho_y.\\n\\\\]\\nIn the \\\\(x\\\\)-layer \\\\(\\\\rho_x=\\\\rho,\\\\rho_y=0\\\\), so\\n\\\\[\\nP=\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)}E,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)=\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty+\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)} .\\n\\\\]\\nThe transformed equations are\\n\\\\[\\n(s+\\\\rho)\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)E=\\\\nu H_y-ikH_x,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mu sH_x=-ikE,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)H_y=\\\\nu E.\\n\\\\]\\nThus\\n\\\\[\\nH_x=-\\\\frac{ik}{\\\\mu s}E,\\\\qquad\\nH_y=\\\\frac{\\\\nu}{\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)}E\\n\\\\]\\nand\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\nu^2=\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)^2\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)\\n      +k^2\\\\frac{s+\\\\rho}{s}.\\n\\\\]\\nThe v2 PML admittance is therefore\\n\\\\[\\nY_{v2}(s,k)=\\\\frac{\\\\nu}{\\\\mu(s+\\\\rho)},\\\\qquad\\nY_{v2}(s,k)^2\\n=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\n\\\\left(\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+\\\\frac{k^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}\\\\right).\\n\\\\]\\n\\nComparing with the physical admittance,\\n\\\\[\\nY_{v2}^2-Y_0^2\\n=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left[\\n\\\\mu(\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)-\\\\varepsilon_D(s))\\n+\\\\frac{k^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}-\\\\frac{k^2}{s^2}\\\\right].\\n\\\\]\\nSince\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)-\\\\varepsilon_D(s)\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\chi\\\\tau\\\\rho}{(1+\\\\tau s)(1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho))}\\n\\\\]\\nand\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{1}{s(s+\\\\rho)}-\\\\frac{1}{s^2}\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{s^2(s+\\\\rho)},\\n\\\\]\\nthe exact mismatch is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\nY_{v2}^2-Y_0^2\\n=-\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\mu^2}\\\\left[\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mu\\\\chi\\\\tau}{(1+\\\\tau s)(1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho))}\\n+\\\\frac{k^2}{s^2(s+\\\\rho)}\\n\\\\right].}\\n\\\\]\\nThis expression is not identically zero for \\\\(\\\\rho>0\\\\).  Hence the v2 model is\\nnot perfectly matched.\\n\\nThe corresponding reflection coefficient is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\nR_{v2}(s,k)=\\n\\\\frac{\\n\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+k^2/s^2}\\n-\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+k^2/[s(s+\\\\rho)]}\\n}{\\n\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_D(s)+k^2/s^2}\\n+\\\\sqrt{\\\\mu\\\\varepsilon_\\\\rho(s)+k^2/[s(s+\\\\rho)]}\\n}.}\\n\\\\]\\nThe square-root branches are those inherited from the outgoing physical and\\ndecaying PML modes.\\n\\n## Interpretation of the mismatch\\n\\nThere are two independent formula-level defects.\\n\\n1. The Debye susceptibility is shifted from\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau s}\\n\\\\quad\\\\text{to}\\\\quad\\n\\\\frac{\\\\chi}{1+\\\\tau(s+\\\\rho)}.\\n\\\\]\\nThis changes the material impedance even at normal incidence \\\\(k=0\\\\), unless\\n\\\\(\\\\chi=0\\\\), \\\\(\\\\tau=0\\\\), or \\\\(\\\\rho=0\\\\).\\n\\n2. The oblique tangential part changes from \\\\(k^2/s^2\\\\) to\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{k^2}{s(s+\\\\rho)}.\\n\\\\]\\nThis remains a mismatch for \\\\(k\\\\ne0\\\\) even in the nondispersive limit\\n\\\\(\\\\chi=0\\\\).\\n\\nThus applying the same covariant derivative \\\\(D_\\\\rho\\\\) to the Debye law is good\\nfor the v2 monotone energy identity, but it is not the Laplace-domain\\nstretched-coordinate continuation of the physical Maxwell--Debye system.\\n\\n## Durable fact candidate\\n\\nClaim summary:\\nThe covariantly damped v2 Maxwell--Debye absorbing-layer model is not perfectly\\nmatched at a planar constant-coefficient \\\\(x\\\\)-PML interface; its squared\\nadmittance differs from the physical Maxwell--Debye admittance by the boxed\\nformula above.\\n\\nDependencies:\\n\\n- `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy`\\n  for the v2 model definition and verified energy identity.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d/codex.events.jsonl:17:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' results/energy_design_v2_report_verified.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"<!-- ITERIS VERIFIED: goal_success verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx assembly verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ -->\\n# Energy Design V2 Report\\n\\nProblem id: `2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration`\\n\\nSource: `sources/energy_functional_problem.tex`\\n\\nStage-2 goal: use the verified edge-PML obstruction for the original\\neight-variable alpha \\\\(=1\\\\) model as input, then construct or propose repaired\\nPML/absorbing-layer formulations and identify a model with a monotone or\\ngenuinely dissipative energy estimate.\\n\\n## Fact Index\\n\\n| fact id | status | verification |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-balance` | verified | `verification/results/verify-20260619T180514214437Z-fact-alpha-1-pec-balance-and-shifted-mag.json` |\\n| `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:edge-pml-linear-obstruction` | verified | `verification/results/verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-.json` |\\n| `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:augmented-gronwall-energy` | verified | `verification/results/verify-20260619T181650715321Z-fact-a-positive-augmented-zeroth-order-e.json` |\\n| `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy` | verified | `verification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json` |\\n\\nProof artifact for the second-stage designs:\\n`artifacts/proofs/stage2_repair_design.md`.\\n\\n## Verified Obstruction From The Old Model\\n\\nThe old alpha \\\\(=1\\\\) source model uses\\n\\\\[\\nE,\\\\ H_x,\\\\ H_y,\\\\ P,\\\\ P_{z,1},\\\\ P_{z,2},\\\\ Q_x,\\\\ Q_y .\\n\\\\]\\nWith\\n\\\\[\\na_x=\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_y-\\\\sigma_x}{\\\\epsilon_0},\\\\qquad\\na_y=\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x-\\\\sigma_y}{\\\\epsilon_0},\\n\\\\]\\nthe shifted magnetic variables\\n\\\\[\\nM_x=Q_x-\\\\mu a_xH_x,\\\\qquad M_y=Q_y-\\\\mu a_yH_y\\n\\\\]\\nsatisfy\\n\\\\[\\nM_{x,t}=a_x\\\\partial_yE-\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_y}{\\\\epsilon_0}M_x,\\\\qquad\\nM_{y,t}=-a_y\\\\partial_xE-\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x}{\\\\epsilon_0}M_y .\\n\\\\]\\n\\nIn an \\\\(x\\\\)-edge PML with constant \\\\(\\\\sigma_x=s>0,\\\\sigma_y=0\\\\), the ansatz\\n\\\\[\\nE=P=P_{z,1}=P_{z,2}=H_y=Q_y=0\\n\\\\]\\nwith spatially constant \\\\(H_x,Q_x\\\\) gives\\n\\\\[\\nM_x=Q_x+\\\\mu\\\\frac{s}{\\\\epsilon_0}H_x=\\\\text{constant}\\n\\\\]\\nand therefore\\n\\\\[\\nH_x(t)=H_x(0)+\\\\frac{M_x(0)}{\\\\mu}t,\\\\qquad\\nQ_x(t)=Q_x(0)-\\\\frac{s}{\\\\epsilon_0}M_x(0)t .\\n\\\\]\\nThe obstruction is the undamped shifted magnetic auxiliary in the edge\\ndirection.  Since this exact solution has \\\\(P=0\\\\), changing only the Debye or\\nfractional polarization law cannot remove it.\\n\\n## Repair 1: Compatibility Restriction\\n\\nFor the old equations, the minimal compatibility condition that kills the\\nverified constant edge mode is\\n\\\\[\\nQ_x(0)+\\\\mu\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x}{\\\\epsilon_0}H_x(0)=0\\n\\\\quad\\\\text{on an \\\\(x\\\\)-edge zero-transverse mode,}\\n\\\\]\\nand symmetrically\\n\\\\[\\nQ_y(0)+\\\\mu\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_y}{\\\\epsilon_0}H_y(0)=0\\n\\\\quad\\\\text{on a \\\\(y\\\\)-edge zero-transverse mode.}\\n\\\\]\\nThis is physically meaningful if the \\\\(Q_i\\\\) are not independent data but\\nhistory variables generated by a PML construction.\\n\\nCandidate energy:\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal E_0=\\\\frac12\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\n\\\\left(\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E^2+\\\\mu H_x^2+\\\\mu H_y^2\\n+\\\\chi^{-1}P^2+P_{z,1}^2+P_{z,2}^2+Q_x^2+Q_y^2\\\\right)\\\\,dxdy .\\n\\\\]\\nIt is positive, and the previous verified result gives\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal E_0'(t)\\\\le C_G\\\\mathcal E_0(t).\\n\\\\]\\n\\nClassification: useful but partial.  In a genuine 2D \\\\(x\\\\)-edge,\\n\\\\[\\nM_{x,t}=-\\\\frac{\\\\sigma_x}{\\\\epsilon_0}\\\\partial_yE,\\n\\\\]\\nso pointwise \\\\(M_x=0\\\\) is not invariant for arbitrary two-dimensional data.\\nThis route removes the verified zero-transverse free mode but does not produce\\na full 2D monotone energy for the old model.\\n\\n## Repair 2: Shifted-Variable MPML Damping\\n\\nKeep the old shifted variables but add edge-positive damping\\n\\\\(\\\\eta_x,\\\\eta_y\\\\ge0\\\\):\\n\\\\[\\nQ_{x,t}=-(b_x+\\\\eta_x)Q_x+\\\\mu(b_x+\\\\eta_x)a_xH_x,\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\nQ_{y,t}=-(b_y+\\\\eta_y)Q_y+\\\\mu(b_y+\\\\eta_y)a_yH_y,\\n\\\\]\\nwhere \\\\(b_i=\\\\sigma_i/\\\\epsilon_0\\\\).  Equivalently,\\n\\\\[\\nM_{x,t}=a_x\\\\partial_yE-(b_y+\\\\eta_x)M_x,\\\\qquad\\nM_{y,t}=-a_y\\\\partial_xE-(b_x+\\\\eta_y)M_y .\\n\\\\]\\n\\nFor the old \\\\(x\\\\)-edge free subsystem this becomes\\n\\\\[\\nH_{x,t}=\\\\frac{M_x}{\\\\mu},\\\\qquad M_{x,t}=-\\\\eta_xM_x .\\n\\\\]\\nIf \\\\(\\\\eta_x>0\\\\), then\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathcal E_{x,\\\\eta}\\n=\\\\frac{\\\\mu}{2}\\\\left|H_x+\\\\frac{M_x}{\\\\mu\\\\eta_x}\\\\right|^2\\n+\\\\frac{c_x}{2}|M_x|^2,\\\\qquad c_x>0,\\n\\\\]\\nis positive and satisfies\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{d}{dt}\\\\mathcal E_{x,\\\\eta}=-c_x\\\\eta_x|M_x|^2\\\\le0 .\\n\\\\]\\n\\nClassification: monotone for the isolated edge free mode and a plausible\\nMPML/CFS repair of the old Jordan block.  In full 2D it still leaves\\n\\\\(M_x\\\\partial_yE\\\\) and \\\\(M_y\\\\partial_xE\\\\) couplings, so the completed theorem\\nwould need derivative, nonlocal, or Baffet-type structure.\\n\\n## Selected Model: Covariantly Damped Maxwell-Debye Layer\\n\\nThe strongest verified constructive result is a modified alpha \\\\(=1\\\\)\\nMaxwell-Debye absorbing-layer model.  Let\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\rho_x,\\\\rho_y\\\\in L^\\\\infty(\\\\Omega),\\\\qquad \\\\rho_x,\\\\rho_y\\\\ge0,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\rho=\\\\rho_x+\\\\rho_y,\\\\qquad D_\\\\rho=\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho .\\n\\\\]\\nThe profiles vanish in the physical region and are positive in the absorbing\\nlayer.\\n\\nThe model is\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty D_\\\\rho E\\n&=\\\\partial_xH_y-\\\\partial_yH_x-D_\\\\rho P,\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_y)H_x&=-\\\\partial_yE,\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\mu(\\\\partial_t+\\\\rho_x)H_y&=\\\\partial_xE,\\\\\\\\\\nP+\\\\tau D_\\\\rho P&=\\\\chi E,\\n\\\\end{aligned}}\\n\\\\]\\nwith PEC boundary condition \\\\(E=0\\\\) on \\\\(\\\\partial\\\\Omega\\\\).\\n\\nThis model removes the independent \\\\(P_{z,i},Q_i\\\\) variables.  The old edge\\nauxiliary mode is therefore absent.  The important design choice is applying\\nthe same covariant derivative \\\\(D_\\\\rho\\\\) to the Debye law; this changes the old\\nsign-indefinite \\\\(EP\\\\) damping term into positive polarization dissipation.\\n\\n## Energy Functional\\n\\nUse\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\mathcal E_\\\\rho(t)=\\\\frac12\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\n\\\\left(\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty E^2+\\\\mu H_x^2+\\\\mu H_y^2+\\\\chi^{-1}P^2\\\\right)\\n\\\\,dxdy .}\\n\\\\]\\nThis energy is positive definite because\\n\\\\(\\\\epsilon_0,\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty,\\\\mu,\\\\chi>0\\\\).\\n\\n## Energy Identity\\n\\nMultiplying the equations by \\\\(E,H_x,H_y\\\\), integrating, and using PEC gives\\nthe usual Maxwell cancellation:\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\int_\\\\Omega(E\\\\partial_xH_y-E\\\\partial_yH_x-H_x\\\\partial_yE+H_y\\\\partial_xE)\\\\,dxdy=0 .\\n\\\\]\\nThe covariant Debye law gives\\n\\\\[\\nE\\\\,D_\\\\rho P\\n=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\chi}\\\\partial_t(P^2)\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\chi}P^2\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}|D_\\\\rho P|^2 .\\n\\\\]\\nTherefore\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\n\\\\frac{d}{dt}\\\\mathcal E_\\\\rho(t)\\n=-\\\\int_\\\\Omega\\\\left(\\n\\\\epsilon_0\\\\epsilon_\\\\infty\\\\rho E^2\\n+\\\\mu\\\\rho_yH_x^2\\n+\\\\mu\\\\rho_xH_y^2\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\rho}{\\\\chi}P^2\\n+\\\\frac{\\\\tau}{\\\\chi}|D_\\\\rho P|^2\\n\\\\right)\\\\,dxdy\\\\le0 .}\\n\\\\]\\nThus\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\mathcal E_\\\\rho(t)\\\\le \\\\mathcal E_\\\\rho(0)\\\\quad\\\\text{for all }t\\\\ge0.}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nClassification: monotone decreasing, dissipative, and uniformly bounded in\\nlong time.  It is a repaired absorbing-layer model, not a proof that the old\\neight-variable unsplit source PML is monotone.\\n\\n## Remaining Open Problems\\n\\n1. Exact perfect matching for the selected covariantly damped model is not\\nproved here.  The verified result is stability and layer dissipation.\\n2. The shifted MPML repair needs a full 2D derivative or nonlocal energy to\\ncontrol \\\\(M_x\\\\partial_yE\\\\) and \\\\(M_y\\\\partial_xE\\\\).\\n3. The compatibility route should be sharpened by Fourier analysis of the\\ntransverse zero-mode projection and by a boundary-compatible definition of the\\nallowed old-model data.\\n4. The fractional case \\\\(0<\\\\alpha<1\\\\) can be added later by replacing the\\nalpha \\\\(=1\\\\) Debye identity with a positive fractional-memory representation;\\nit cannot remove the old edge obstruction by itself because that obstruction\\nhas \\\\(P=0\\\\).\\n\\n## Assembly\\n\\nThe old-model obstruction is supplied by\\n`fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:edge-pml-linear-obstruction`.\\nThe old-model algebra and Gronwall fallback are supplied by\\n`fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-balance` and\\n`fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:augmented-gronwall-energy`.\\n\\nThe constructive second-stage result is supplied by\\n`fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy`:\\nthe modified covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye absorbing layer has a positive\\nmonotone energy identity.  This answers the second-stage goal by identifying\\nthe old obstruction, comparing three repairs, and selecting a verified repaired\\nmodel with a long-time-uniform dissipative energy estimate.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-covariantly-damped-maxwell-d/codex.events.jsonl:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"covariantly-damped-debye-energy|v2|D_rho|D_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\rho|rho_x|rho_y\\\\\\\" memory/facts artifacts results verification/results sources -S\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"results/VERIFICATION_STATUS.json:3:  \\\"target_artifact\\\": \\\"results/energy_design_v2_report.md\\\",\\nresults/VERIFICATION_STATUS.json:8:  \\\"verified_artifact\\\": \\\"results/energy_design_v2_report_verified.md\\\"\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:11:File: ctexbackend.cfg 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Backend configuration file (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:23:Document Class: ctexart 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Chinese adapter for class article (C\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:26:Package: ctexhook 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Document and package hooks (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:29:Package: ctexpatch 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Patching commands (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:45:File: ctexopts.cfg 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Option configuration file (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:65:File: ctex-engine-xetex.def 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 XeLaTeX adapter (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:137:Package: fontspec 2024/05/11 v2.9e Font selection for XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:140:Package: fontspec-xetex 2024/05/11 v2.9e Font selection for XeLaTeX and LuaLaTe\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:158:Package: fontenc 2021/04/29 v2.0v Standard LaTeX package\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:181:File: ctex-scheme-chinese-article.def 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Chinese scheme for art\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:185:File: ctex-name-utf8.cfg 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Caption with encoding UTF-8 (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:188:File: ctex-fontset-mac.def 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 macOS fonts definition (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:192:File: ctex-fontset-macold.def 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 macOS fonts definition for Yos\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:233:File: ctex.cfg 2022/07/14 v2.5.10 Configuration file (CTEX)\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:236:Package: amsmath 2024/11/05 v2.17t AMS math features\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:240:Package: amstext 2021/08/26 v2.01 AMS text\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:243:File: amsgen.sty 1999/11/30 v2.0 generic functions\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:252:Package: amsopn 2022/04/08 v2.04 operator names\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:314:Package: amsthm 2020/05/29 v2.20.6\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:452:Package: nameref 2023-11-26 v2.56 Cross-referencing by name of section\\nsources/energy_ansatz_notes.log:466:Package: etoolbox 2025/02/11 v2.5l e-TeX tools for LaTeX (JAW)\\nmemory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:2:fact_id: fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched\\nmemory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:7:  - fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy\\nmemory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:12:claim_summary: \\\"The v2 covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye layer is not perfectly matched.\\\"\\nmemory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:18:For a planar x-interface with constant layer coefficient rho_x=rho>0, rho_y=0, Laplace parameter Re s>0, and tangential Fourier number k_y, the physical Maxwell-Debye admittance is Y0^2=A(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2), where A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s).  The v2 covariantly damped model has Yrho^2=A_rho(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s(s+rho)), where A_rho(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau(s+rho)).  Hence Yrho^2-Y0^2=-rho[chi tau/(mu(1+tau(s+rho))(1+tau s))+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+rho))], which is generically nonzero.  Therefore the interface reflection coefficient (Y0-Yrho)/(Y0+Yrho) is generically nonzero: the model is dissipative but not perfectly matched.  Full derivation: artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md.\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx.json:6:  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Read .iteris/goal_prompt.txt and execute the second-stage Iteris goal: analyze the verified obstruction in results/energy_functional_report_verified.md without treating it as final success; identify the old-model edge-PML linear-growth term; propose at least three repairs including compatibility restriction, shifted-variable reformulation, and modified damping/PML model; derive candidate energies, positivity, and energy derivative classifications; select the most promising repaired model; write results/energy_design_v2_report.md with obstruction, modified models, exact best-candidate equations, energy functional, positivity proof, energy identity or inequality, classification, and open problems; pass assembly and goal-success verification.\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx.json:10:  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Correct. The source goal is a stage-2 constructive task, not a universal proof that the original eight-variable source PML is monotone: it requires analyzing the verified old edge-PML obstruction, proposing repaired or modified formulations, deriving energies/positivity/derivative classifications, selecting a promising repaired model, and writing results/energy_design_v2_report.md. The terminal report covers that scope. It identifies the undamped shifted magnetic edge mode as the old-model obstruction, gives three repair routes (compatibility restriction, shifted-variable MPML damping, and a covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye absorbing layer), classifies the first two as partial, and selects the covariantly damped model. The selected model's positivity and monotone energy identity are supported by the cited verified fact and by the displayed calculation: PEC cancels the Maxwell flux, and the covariant Debye identity converts E D_rho P into the time derivative of chi^{-1}P^2/2 plus nonnegative rho P^2/chi and tau |D_rho P|^2/chi dissipation. The report does not overclaim exact perfect matching or a monotone energy for the old eight-variable model.\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx.json:19:    \\\"results/energy_design_v2_report.md\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx.json:21:    \\\"memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-covariantly-damped-debye-energy.md\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx.json:31:    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy\\\"\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023507094543Z-goal_success-read-.iteris-goal_prompt.tx.json:34:  \\\"target_artifact\\\": \\\"results/energy_design_v2_report.md\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043300709633Z-assembly-stage-3-report-assembles-the-pe.json:32:    \\\"artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:29:      \\\"location\\\": \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:33:      \\\"location\\\": \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:50:    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched: referenced fact status is 'submitted', not 'verified'\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:51:    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched: referenced fact lacks a verification link\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:61:    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T043309704737Z-assembly-stage-3-terminal-report-results.json:65:  