iginal source model are verified and are used only as context/motivation for the repair; the artifact clearly states that the covariantly damped model is a modified absorbing model, not an algebraically identical proof for the old eight-variable unsplit PML and not a proof of exact perfect matching.\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:16:    \\\"memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-covariantly-damped-debye-energy.md\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T022411192181Z-fact-the-covariantly-damped-alpha-1-maxw.json:27:    \\\"fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:covariantly-damped-debye-energy\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:10:  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Correct. The target report is supported at assembly scope. The old-model shifted-variable identities and exact edge-PML linear-growth obstruction are backed by the verified alpha1 algebra and edge-obstruction facts. The compatibility and shifted-MPML repair discussions are presented only as partial or edge-subsystem repairs, matching the stage-2 proof artifact and not overclaiming a full 2D monotone theorem for the old eight-variable model. The selected covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye absorbing-layer model is backed by the verified covariantly-damped-debye-energy fact: under nonnegative time-independent layer profiles and PEC boundary condition, its positive energy has the displayed monotone identity. The report explicitly states that exact perfect matching and a full old-model monotone result remain open.\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:16:    \\\"results/energy_design_v2_report.md\\\",\\nverification/results/verify-20260620T023007094217Z-assembly-assemble-verified-facts-to-answ.json:22:    \\\"memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-covariantly-